id: 14
hanzi: 绳子
pinyin: shéng zi
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: rope; cord; string; twine; cordage
  es: cuerda; soga; cordel; maroma; lazo de cáñamo o fibra

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a strong, thick cord made by twisting together strands of hemp, sisal, nylon, or other fibers | cuerda resistente fabricada retorciendo filamentos de cáñamo, nailon u otras fibras | 系紧绳子 (tie the rope tightly)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 登山队员将坚固的绳子牢牢系在崖壁的岩石扣上，确保下撤过程万无一失。 | Dēngshān duìyuán jiāng jiāngù de shéngzi láoláo jì zài yábì de yánshí kòu shàng, quèbǎo xiàchè guòchéng wànwú-yìshī. | The mountaineer tied the sturdy rope securely to the rock carabiner on the cliff face, ensuring flawless safety during the descent. | El alpinista aseguró la recia cuerda al mosquetón de roca en la pared del risco, garantizando la máxima seguridad durante el descenso.
  #2 | 摸到象尾巴的盲人断言大象不过是一根绳子，这种各执一词的武断正是狭隘认知的真实写照。 | Mōdào xiàng wěiba de mángrén duànyán dàxiàng búguò shì yì gēn shéngzi, zhè zhǒng gèzhíyìcí de wǔduàn zhèng shì xiá'ài rènzhī de zhēnshí xièzhào. | The blind man who touched the elephant's tail asserted an elephant was merely a rope; such dogmatic insistence is a true portrait of narrow cognition. | El ciego que palpó la cola del paquidermo afirmó que el elefante no era más que una soga; tal terquedad dogmática retrata fielmente las limitaciones de la mente estrecha.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  一根绳子 | a rope (classifier: 根)
  系紧绳子 | tie a rope tightly
  解开绳子 | untie or loosen a rope
  拉动绳子 | pull a rope
  粗麻绳子 | thick hemp rope
  跳绳子 | skip rope; jump rope

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  绳锯木断 | shéng jù mù duàn | rope saws through wood with persistent friction; perseverance wins
  规绳矩墨 | guī shéng jǔ mò | compass, rope, carpenter's square and chalk line; strict standards
  结绳记事 | jié shéng jì shì | tie knots in cords to record events (ancient mnemonic practice)
  绳之以法 | shéng zhī yǐ fǎ | restrain by law; bring a criminal to justice

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  绳 | shéng | rope; cord; restrain; standard | cuerda; soga; normar | 纟 | silk / thread | 纟 (silk thread, twisted cordage) | 黾 (mǐn, toad / water frog) | 11 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: twisted silk threads 纟 combined with 黾, portraying thick cordage braided like sinuous amphibians. | Strands of strong woven silk (纟) braided with the tenacity of a water toad (黾) form an unbreakable rope (绳). | Hebras de seda resistente (纟) trenzadas con la tenacidad de un anfibio (黾) forjan una recia soga (绳). | 35 | VMRXU | 繩
  子 | zi | child; son; noun suffix | hijo; niño; sufijo nominal | 子 | child / son | 子 (swaddled baby waving arms) | "" | 3 | 单一结构 | Ancient oracle bone pictogram of an infant waving arms with swaddled legs. Used universally as a nominalizing noun suffix. | An energetic young baby (子) waves its tiny arms happily above its swaddling blanket. | Un infante despierto (子) mueve los bracitos con alegría sobre su pañal de abrigo. | 214 | ND | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Twisted strands of durable fiber (绳) form the everyday household cord and rope (绳子).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Hebras de fibra trenzadas con firmeza (绳) forman la soga o cuerda cotidiana (绳子).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient Chinese civilization prior to written characters, 结绳记事 (knotting cords to record transactions) was the primal mnemonic system. In carpentry, the ink-marker rope (墨绳) symbolized unbending moral standards and legal restraint (绳之以法).
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising 2nd tone followed by neutral tone: 'shéng zi' (35-neutral). Rise smoothly on 'shéng' and pronounce 'zi' with a light, clipped release.

