semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 绳子 is the standard everyday noun for cord or rope made of braided fibers.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 绳子 vs. 线 | xiàn | 绳子 refers to thick, load-bearing braided ropes or cords, whereas 线 denotes thin, fine sewing thread, string, or electrical wire (缝衣线, 电线).
    2 | 绳子 vs. 缆绳 | lǎnshéng | 绳子 is generic and everyday, while 缆绳 refers specifically to heavy-duty industrial or maritime steel cables and mooring hawsers.
    3 | 绳子 vs. 绳索 | shéngsuǒ | 绳子 is colloquial and common (跳绳子, 绑绳子), while 绳索 is formal, technical, and literary, frequently used in mountaineering and rescue reports.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 一根看似平凡的绳子，在劳动者的手中却能化作连接重物与希望的纽带。无论是在崇山峻岭间攀援，还是在田间地头捆扎丰收的麦穗，结实的绳子始终默默承受着巨大的拉力，见证着人类勤劳质朴的岁月。 | Yì gēn kànsì píngfán de shéngzi, zài láodòngzhě de shǒuzhōng què néng huàzuò liánjiē zhòngwù yǔ xīwàng de niǔdài. Wúlùn shì zài chóngshān-jùnlǐng jiān pānyuán, háishì zài tiánjiān-dìtóu kǔnzā fēngshōu de màisuì, jiēshi de shéngzi shǐzhōng mòmò chéngshòu zhe jùdà de lālì, jiànzhèng zhe rénlèi qínláo zhìpǔ de suìyuè. | A seemingly ordinary rope in the hands of laborers transforms into a bond linking heavy burdens and hope. Whether ascending rugged peaks or bundling golden wheat in autumn fields, the sturdy rope silently bears immense tension, witnessing human diligence. | Una cuerda en apariencia modesta se convierte en manos de los trabajadores en lazo de esperanza y esfuerzo. Ya sea trepando riscos escarpados o atando gavillas doradas de trigo, la recia soga resiste en silencio la tensión, dando fe del fecundo quehacer humano.
  #2 | “绳锯木断，水滴石穿”，这句古老的格言借由柔软的绳子能锯断坚硬木料的自然现象，阐明了持之以恒的深刻哲理。只要锚定目标并日积月累地付出心血，哪怕微不足道的力量也能创造出令人惊叹的奇迹。 | 'Shéng jù mù duàn, shuǐ dī shí chuān', zhè jù gǔlǎo de gèyán jièyóu róuruǎn de shéngzi néng jùduàn jiānyìng mùliào de zìrán xiànxiàng, chǎnmíng le chízhīyǐhéng de shēnkè zhélǐ. Zhǐyào máodìng mùbiāo bìng rìjī-yuèlěi de fùchū xīnxuè, nǎpà wēibùzúdào de lìliàng yě néng chuàngzào chū lìngrén jīngtàn de qíjì. | 'A rope saws through wood and dripping water penetrates stone'—this ancient proverb utilizes the phenomenon of soft cords sawing timber to demonstrate the power of perseverance. Anchoring goals and exerting continuous effort transforms minuscule forces into miracles. | 'La cuerda corta el madero y la gota horada la piedra': esta sabia máxima se vale de la soga para ilustrar el poder de la perseverancia. Fijando un rumbo y aunando desvelos día tras día, las fuerzas en apariencia insignificantes acaban engendrando admirables portentos.
